<speak>
<s>This is your briefing for <say-as interpret-as="date" format="dmy">22092026</say-as>.</s>
<break time="1s"/>
<prosody rate="95%">
<s>Britain's committed a Royal Air Force tanker to refuel Saudi jets striking Houthi forces in Yemen... and that draws it back into a war whose last air campaign killed thousands of Yemeni civilians.</s> <s>Aerial refuelling is what lets Saudi aircraft reach deep into Yemen, so this "limited" support is what makes the campaign possible.</s> <s>It follows the Houthi seizure of Mocha port and nearby Red Sea islands beside the Bab al-Mandeb strait, and Yemeni civilians will bear the cost.</s>
</prosody>
<p>
<s>In politics.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>China's expelled Zhang Youxia, vice-chairman of the Central Military Commission, and Liu Zhenli, chief of its Joint Staff, for forming factions and taking bribes.</s> <s>The body that commands the People's Liberation Army now has just two members, and it's the deepest purge of the uniformed leadership since the Mao era.</s> <s>Loyalty to Xi Jinping, not command experience, is now the test for leading the world's largest army, and no one yet knows how that changes its judgment in a crisis.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>In Brazil, two separate polls put Flávio Bolsonaro within a single point of President Lula in a possible runoff, inside the margin of error.</s> <s>His father, Jair Bolsonaro, is barred from running, yet the movement has carried its base over to the son almost intact.</s> <s>Latin America's largest democracy faces a coin-flip election that'll shape both its Amazon policy and its place in BRICS.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Pakistani hospitals have been ordered to clear beds, postpone elective surgery indefinitely and suspend all staff leave before an opposition march planned for <say-as interpret-as="date" format="dmy">27092026</say-as>.</s> <s>Within twenty-four hours, police detained eight relatives of jailed former prime minister Imran Khan, whose party, Pakistan Tehreek-e-Insaf, is leading the march.</s> <s>The state's preparing for mass casualties before a single protester has set out... and it's unclear whether that order is a forecast or a warning.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Satellite analysis by the research group Forensic Architecture shows at least five Israeli-backed Palestinian militias operating from compounds beside Israeli army bases in Gaza.</s> <s>Those compounds have been reinforced with earth berms, barracks and fences, and it's the old model of rule by proxy, the same one South Lebanon's Israeli-armed militia followed until two thousand.</s> <s>Nearly a year into the ceasefire, Palestinians living beside them face armed men answerable to no Palestinian authority and to no court.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>A munitions depot blast near Aleppo has injured four people, after three earlier explosions killed thirty.</s> <s>Syria's rebuilt army is moving weapons from several former factions into decades-old depots, where ageing ordnance kept without cooling or humidity control can set off a chain reaction.</s> <s>Until those stockpiles are audited and made safe, the neighbourhoods around them are living beside a slow-burning hazard.</s>
</p>
<p>
<s>On the economy.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>Nigeria is Africa's top oil producer, yet for decades it imported almost all of its petrol and diesel.</s> <s>Aliko Dangote's refinery now supplies most of both, and that's breaking a colonial-era pattern of exporting raw crude and buying back finished fuel, a pattern that drained the naira for years.</s> <s>But a single refinery owned by one billionaire now shapes a nation's currency and fuel supply, and that's a new kind of dependence.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>A Ukrainian drone strike on <say-as interpret-as="date" format="dmy">20092026</say-as> set both main crude units alight at the refinery that supplies forty percent of Moscow's fuel, halting it.</s> <s>Gazprom Neft stations have since halved the fuel limit per purchase, from sixty litres to thirty.</s> <s>Now France's Emmanuel Macron says he's discussed a mutual halt on energy strikes with Donald Trump... which would trade away Kyiv's sharpest pressure on Russian oil revenue for new air-defence interceptors.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Egypt's state broadcaster, known by the name of its Cairo tower, Maspero, has cleared almost one hundred and forty billion Egyptian pounds of debt it's piled up since the nineteen-eighties.</s> <s>Forty-four of its assets, worth eighteen billion pounds, changed hands, while fifty-one billion in interest and penalties was written off and state land covered another seventy billion.</s> <s>Much of the debt hasn't vanished so much as moved from one state ledger to another.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Jamaica hosts the International Seabed Authority, the body writing the rules for mining the ocean floor more than a thousand metres down.</s> <s>Miners want cobalt, copper, manganese and nickel for batteries and wind turbines, but sediment plumes and lost habitat could thin out the food chain that Jamaican fishers depend on.</s> <s>They live closest to the regulator of any fishing community on earth, and they say they still don't know what's being decided.</s>
</p>
<p>
<s>In science.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>The Americas have lost the measles-free status they earned in twenty sixteen, and cases have hit a record.</s> <s>Herd immunity needs about ninety-five percent vaccine coverage, and several countries have slipped below that line, just as the World Cup moved millions of fans across borders.</s> <s>Children in low-coverage communities across Latin America are the ones most at risk now.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>The central Pacific stood three point oh seven degrees Celsius above average on <say-as interpret-as="date" format="dmy">19092026</say-as>, just a hundredth of a degree short of the record.</s> <s>This super El Niño is developing faster than any on record, and El Niños temporarily push global temperatures above the long-term warming trend.</s> <s>Whether or not it breaks the record, what matters is where that heat lands next, on harvests, fisheries and humid cities already near the limits of what the body can bear.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>A draft US executive order would let a single panel, including budget chief Russell Vought, reject any of the sixty-four thousand grants the National Institutes of Health awards each year.</s> <s>That agency's forty-seven billion dollar budget is bigger than the next ten research funders combined, and since the Second World War, scientists reviewing each other's work have decided what it pays for.</s> <s>Every grant would need the panel's unanimous sign-off, so political appointees would decide what American medicine gets to study.</s>
</p>
<p>
<s>In technology.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>Twenty nations, among them Germany and South Africa, have signed a pact at the UN seeking a global body that would convene states when AI capabilities cross set thresholds.</s> <s>The two powers that build most frontier models, the US and China, refused to sign... much as the early nuclear age had rules that meant little until the leading powers joined.</s> <s>Nobody's yet shown how a pact can bind labs whose own governments stay outside it.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Ireland's Data Protection Commission will fine Google four hundred and three million euros over how it processed location data, ending an inquiry that took six years.</s> <s>Under the European Union's one-stop-shop rule, Dublin leads enforcement against most American tech giants because they've based their European headquarters there, and critics have long called it too slow.</s> <s>The real test is whether the fine changes how location data is collected, or just becomes a cost of doing business.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>The Canadian province of British Columbia is suing OpenAI, saying the company's own reviewers urged a police referral about a user before a shooting in Tumbler Ridge that killed nine.</s> <s>According to the suit, the company's leaders only deactivated the account, and it's rare for a government, rather than grieving families, to take an AI company to court over a duty to warn.</s> <s>If the claim holds, chatbot makers could be held responsible for acting on what their users tell them.</s>
</p>
<break time="1s"/>
<prosody rate="90%">
<s>That's your briefing.</s>
</prosody>
